From a9279d2aea0dd234fa590ab92c9117d30b2d73c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:06:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] build.py: usb_midi_last, usb_iad and usb_serial; a USB
 descriptor test

usb_midi_last moves the MIDI function behind the streaming interfaces (AC, AS, [ASO], MIDI).
Bisected on macOS 15.8.1: this ordering is what makes the USB audio input enumerate; keeping
MIDI out of the AC header's collection alone (FELUCCA_UAC_AC_COLLECT) is not enough.
(hugelton/Felucca#67, kmplngj/Felucca#532)

usb_iad gives the audio function an IAD covering AC + AS only, with the misc/IAD device class
(EF 02 01, bcdUSB 2.00). It is descriptor hygiene, not a host fix: the plain no-IAD build also
enumerates on macOS, Windows 11, Linux, Android and iPadOS. It wants usb_midi_last so that the
interfaces it names (AC + AS) stay contiguous.

usb_serial names the device's serial number string (default: the package identity), so a host
tells firmwares sharing VID/PID 1209:0001 apart.

tests/usb_desc_test.c checks the descriptors byte by byte on the host across the layout matrix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
